            "scenario": "SECTION B -Answer ONE question only.",
            "text": "People are born to be free but law interferes with their freedom. Explain the two reasons law interferes with the freedom of the individual?",
            "modelAnswer": "Two reasons law interferes with individual freedom:\n(1) To protect the rights of others - one person's freedom ends where another's begins; law limits individual liberty to prevent harm (e.g. laws against assault, trespass, defamation); society cannot function if every individual acts without restraint.\n(2) To promote the public good / collective welfare - collective interests sometimes override individual liberty for the benefit of society as a whole (e.g. taxation compels individuals to contribute to public services; compulsory vaccination protects public health; town planning laws restrict use of private land).\n\nJustifiability: the 1999 Constitution permits derogation from fundamental rights only under specified lawful conditions (s.45). Students should explain both reasons fully with examples."
